Peugeot has given its 508 series of  facelift both technically and in terms  of design the all road models been given  an even more striking front end we're  taking the 508 rxh diesel hybrid out for  a spin the 2-liter engine packs 120  kilowatts under the hood with support at  the rear axle from a 27 kilowatt  electric motor that means the rxh can go  100 kilometers on only 4 litres of  diesel  the radiator grill is even more steeply  raked but the lion emblem is still what  catches the eye  although the rxh looks like a tough  off-road station wagon the base version  is really very sumptuously and  luxuriously equipped for instance the  panoramic sunroof comes as standard  the other special features of the 508  rxh are higher road clearance striking  running lights and coated wheel wells in  addition to chrome trim on the front and  rear bumpers  we're testing a car with a six-speed  Automatic transmission which boosts the  508 rxh hybrid to 100 kilometres an hour  in 8.5 seconds  it has a maximum speed of 213 km/h the  starting price for a basic rxh hybrid is  forty-three thousand six hundred and  fifty euros in Germany  shada finding our test driver Matta  squad says it's a shame that the hybrid  only has a power consumption indicator  rather than a standard tachometer and  the steering is typically French meaning  you can still feel the road even though  it's not as stiff as other cars  nevertheless in terms of driving the  automatic transmission takes too long to  switch between gears Matty says the car  is already a bit ponderous and the  transmission makes a quick getaway even  less likely even after su won't be  hindered mine rushes for comment Suzette  leash the hybrid drive technology is  located under the floor of the cargo  area this is where the electric motor  and batteries are housed that turn the  car into an all wheel drive vehicle  no space is sacrificed to make the car a  hybrid the storage areas volume ranges  from four hundred to one thousand three  hundred and sixty liters that means when  rear seats have been folded down the rxh  has about two hundred and forty liters  less cargo space than the classic diesel  version a plus point however is the  flush cargo Lib at the rear  Matis says the interior is well done all  the materials are soft and the  touchscreen display is better here than  in other purges some he says are  extremely reflective this one is  relatively easy to read even when  there's plenty of light coming through  the panoramic roof which is another one  of his favorite features and there's  more  the rxh isn't just luxurious it's chock  full of helpful gizmos front and rear  parking assist cruise control and a  blind spot assistants are available in  the standard version  and the driver can shift using paddles  on the steering wheel  also standard are heated seats for the  driver and front-passenger  the blend of off-road ruggedness and  interior comfort is impressive but the  hybrid drivetrain is only available in  the rather expensive rxh version of the  508  not it says he likes the new front end  of the Peugeot 508 far more than the old  one whether the car is a sedan a station  wagon all the rxh and the hybrid version  stacks up well in terms of what it  offers in fuel savings yet the vehicle  is exorbitantly priced he says in fact  it may be worth it to look at a diesel  or even a less economical  gasoline-powered model Ben Cena
 

